{"kind":"report","text":"Changes are needed in native Jam source at 654e57098eff014e6d48b7d4c766bffa2a8f3d1f, tree 061bd170b5ef393e96d57010cbdc442ac1e1f41f. The complete receiving-main-relative review covers all 37 changed paths against 990dcbf3ffd15d44c9fccdd88c671866dd5e7218. This is the assigned Source/evidence report, not a guarded merge approval or fulfillment of full Jam request73d/promise1341.\n\nFour P2 corrections are tracked:\n- Solo length uses subjects.configuration, but the staged native judge supplies the literal key also.configuration. The configured limit reads the wrong subject. Correct the binding and verify eligible within-limit and above-limit cases. Request48633ee979e81c77ccae906ecaf249f12d492f59.\n- nativeHistory rejects !page.complete before following page.next. The native SDK uses complete=false with next for ordinary continuation pages. Valid multi-page histories fail before the declared budgets. Preserve frontier, chain, signature, cursor and budget checks while collecting a complete terminal history. Requestdbe5b0dd8e8d981c863718d6af4483d682e3c4dc.\n- nativeBar clips a supported note at the current bar and excludes its continuation from the next bar. Positive late offsets and release tails also cross frame boundaries. Render overlapping waveform intervals without narrowing the existing codec or restarting note state. Request186b4a6d9de9d1bb5012eadce7dc52a1268d9bb8.\n- Unlocked model callbacks can overwrite active BrowserCustody after a newer native follow-up becomes terminal. An older musician request can return as active, and known provider phases can regress. Interpretation then finds its old contribution already consumed, while the original-digest fence prevents a new signature. Use expected active identity/revision and monotonic provider transitions. Preserve late answers in their own history and retain the different-unknown-original fence. Request003082fb84aab46b58764208ac75a24346d3e3a2.\n\nThese findings follow the supported Source p